  "readingHtml": "<h1>The Future of Space Tourism</h1><div class=\"subtitle\">Will you travel to space?</div><p><span class=\"para-label\">A.</span>In the future, traveling to space will not just be for astronauts. Companies are working hard to <b>establish</b> a new industry: space tourism. Next year, they <b>are going to launch</b> the first commercial flights. By 2030, ordinary people <b>will be orbiting</b> the Earth in luxury space hotels.</p><p><span class=\"para-label\">B.</span>However, this type of travel <b>requires</b> strict rules. You <b>have to</b> be in good health. You <b>must not</b> have heart problems. Space is full of <b>hazards</b>, such as space debris. While you <b>are flying</b>, you <b>must</b> wear a special suit. Passengers <b>should</b> also train for a few days before the flight.</p><p><span class=\"para-label\">C.</span>Humans <b>are not adapted</b> to zero gravity. In space, your body <b>will undergo</b> many changes. You might feel <b>isolated</b> or homesick. But most people say they <b>will manage</b> to <b>survive</b> the journey because the view of Earth is unforgettable. Would you <b>be allowed to</b> pay millions of dollars for a ticket? Only time will tell.</p>",
